<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>AdrLine</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Elements</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">AdrLine</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong><code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code> (AddressLine)</strong> is the free-format text element inside the ISO 20022 <code>&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</code> block, carrying up to <strong>70 characters per occurrence</strong>. Its cardinality defines the address format: up to 7 occurrences in the legacy unstructured format, capped at <strong>[0..2] in hybrid</strong> (CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex §0.31), and prohibited entirely in fully structured addresses.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How AdrLine works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>In hybrid format the two permitted lines give 140 characters for residual content — and the No-Duplication Rule applies: anything carried in a structured element must not be repeated in <code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code>. The unstructured pattern (7 × 70 = 490 characters) is decommissioned for newly initiated payments on 15 November 2026.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex §0.31 / p5 and §3 footnote / p6-3; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §3.4.1–§3.4.3, §17.1.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Hybrid usage — one residual line beside the mandatory pair:</p></div>
<div class="code-block"><pre><span class="tag">&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;PstCd&gt;</span>6011<span class="tag">&lt;/PstCd&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;TwnNm&gt;</span>WELLINGTON<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Ctry&gt;</span>NZ<span class="tag">&lt;/Ctry&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;AdrLine&gt;</span>169 CUBA STREET<span class="tag">&lt;/AdrLine&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/PstlAdr&gt;</span></pre></div> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 deadline — the structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
